# Patient chart management — review guide

## Backend contract

- `GET /api/patient-chart/patients/:patientId/attachments?page=1&limit=8`
  now returns `{ data, pagination }` and performs `skip`/`take` in Prisma.
- `DELETE /api/patient-chart/attachments/:attachmentId` is ADMIN-only. It removes
  the attachment record and then attempts to remove its scoped patient-chart file.
- Uploaded charts remain organized under `uploads/patient-charts/patient-{patientId}/`.

## Frontend

- The Patient Chart page now provides a selected-patient control rail, explicit
  upload queue, document library, view/delete controls, and a destructive-action
  confirmation dialog.
- Both the patient directory and the chart file library use server responses and
  the shared Pagination component; no document list is sliced in the browser.
- The Medical Charts tab in patient history requests its active page from the
  same server-side list endpoint and uses its returned total for the chart count.

